      "question": "Why does this circular conflict with our policy?",
      "id": "inv_944062ab2f5b",
      "intent": "explain",
      "summary": "The SEBI circular (D6) conflicts with POL-001 because it imposes different timing and treatment for unpaid securities across multiple provisions. Specifically: the circular caps the maximum period at five trading days while POL-001 \u00a75.1 requires seven trading days; the circular requires the trading member to \u201cgive reasonable notice to the client\u201d before invoking pledge/liquidation while POL-001 \u00a76.1 allows sale and notification after the sale; and the circular forbids allowing client exposure on pledged unpaid securities while POL-001 \u00a75.3 permits it. The workspace records these four specific conflicts for D6.",
